    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 25 tests pass, including the two new Cp15 tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `membershipTier` field to the owner response: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nSince the tier is derivable at response time from two fields already stored on the `Owner` entity (`namesakeCount` and `email`), no new pipeline step or persisted column was needed \u2014 I computed it in the response mapping:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that emits `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and email is non-blank, else `\"BRONZE\"`. The null-safe `Integer.valueOf(0).equals(...)` guard means a missing count also yields `BRONZE`.\n\nThis flows automatically through both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response (both use `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`), matching the tests which read the field back via GET.",
